P2-WINDOWS W7 — page:driving/RouteEfficiency — WinUI 3 / Fluent parity port
============================================================================
Web source : web/src/features/driving/pages/RouteEfficiencyPage.tsx (route /route-efficiency)
Output     : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/RouteEfficiencyPage/
             (repo convention = C#-markup feature-views, not Features/*.xaml; see sibling done pages
              RegenEfficiencyPage / TripPlannerPage. The generated prompt's path
              apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Driving does not exist in-repo.)
Nav        : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs —
             PageFactory.Register("RouteEfficiency", static () => new FeatureViews.Driving.RouteEfficiencyPage())
             (RouteTable already maps Page("RouteEfficiency","route-efficiency",TripsDriving,…) at
              TeslaSync.App.Core/Navigation/RouteTable.cs:290 — no route entry added)
Strings    : apps/windows/Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw already carry 18 of the 19 manifest
             translation.routeEfficiency.* / translation.common.noData keys (catalog-generated). The one key the
             web i18n itself never defines (routeEfficiency.comparison.aria — the web uses an inline t() English
             fallback) resolves through ILocalizer's English-fallback path, the same precedent the sibling
             TripPlannerPage (tripPlanner.disclaimer / tripPlanner.notFeasible) follows. Every visible literal is
             sourced by key; none hardcoded.

Files:
  feature-views/RouteEfficiencyPage/RouteEfficiencyPage.Model.cs      (parsers + snapshot + feed iface + EmptyFeed + display records + projection + registration + diagnostics)
  feature-views/RouteEfficiencyPage/RouteEfficiencyPage.Source.cs     (generated C# client GET adapter: RouteEfficiencyClientFeed)
  feature-views/RouteEfficiencyPage/RouteEfficiencyPage.ViewModel.cs  (INotifyPropertyChanged data holder + state matrix + units)
  feature-views/RouteEfficiencyPage/RouteEfficiencyPage.cs            (WinUI 3 UserControl, Fluent + design tokens)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/RouteEfficiencyPageTests.cs        (34 headless tests)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj                      (link the 3 UI-free files; the WinUI view is build-only)

Data sources (P1/S8 INotifyPropertyChanged VM → generated C# client, web hook name kept at the C# call site):
  useRouteEfficiency -> RouteEfficiencyClientFeed.FetchAsync, ApiRequest("get_api_v1_analytics_route_efficiency",
                        Query{ vehicle_id, start?, end? }) — GET /analytics/route-efficiency
                        (operation id = Operations.Analytics.RouteEfficiency)
  useSelectedVehicle / range -> the feed is pre-scoped with vehicleId + start/end at construction (same seam as the
                        sibling RegenEfficiencyClientFeed); the view binds only the resolved snapshot.
Reused W3 component surfaces: TsGlassPanel, TsAnimatedNumber, TsStatCard-equivalent tiles, TsBadge, TsMetricBar,
  TsChartContainer + TsBarChart (the native recharts BarChart wrapper), TsEmptyState, TsQueryError, TsSkeleton,
  TsDataFreshness, TsFadeIn, PageTitle/Subhead/SectionTitle/Caption/Text typography.
Units (P1/S5): SI read from the API (Wh/km efficiency, km distance); converted only at the display boundary in
  RouteEfficiencyProjection — Wh/km→Wh/mi via *1.609344 (web toEfficiencyDisplay) and meters→display via
  UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi + UnitLabels.Label (no non-SI stored/computed).
Live data: none (web page uses a TanStack-Query read, no useLiveX/SSE), so no SSE subscription / staleness chip
  beyond the standard data-freshness header (ADR-013 live path n/a).
Scope note: the web page renders <AIRouteEfficiencySuggestions/> (an AI-gated, withAiFeature-wrapped surface). That
  surface is its own already-shipped parity unit (shared-surfaces/AIRouteEfficiencySuggestions.*) and is NOT one of
  this page's 29 manifest parity items (data sources = only useRouteEfficiency; panels = 4; charts = 2), so it is
  out of scope here and intentionally not re-embedded — mirroring how TripPlannerPage delegated its sibling W3
  surfaces rather than re-owning them.

